{title: 079 - O Love of God, How Strong and True!}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #079 • OMBERSLEY • 16.15}
{lyricist: Horatius Bonar}
{composer: William H. Gladstone}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 79}
{meta: tune OMBERSLEY}
{meta: meter 16.15}
{meta: category God the Father - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]O love of [F/C]God, how [G7/B]strong and [C]true! Eternal, [F]and yet [Dm]ever [G]new;
[C]Uncomprehended and [Dm]unbought, [C/E]Beyond [Em/G]all [G7]knowledge [F]and [C/G]all [G7]thought.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]O love [F/C]of [G7]God, [C]how deep [F]and great,
[C]Far deeper [G7]than [C]man's deepest [F]hate;
[C]Self-fed, [Em]self-kindled [F]like [G7]the [C/G]light,
[C]Changeless, eternal, [G7]infinite.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]We read [F/C]thee [G7]best [C]in Him [F]who cam
[C]To bear [F/C]for [G7]us [C]the cross [F]of shame;
[C]Sent [Em]by [G7]the [Dm]Father [Em/G]from [Am]on [C/G]high,
[C]Our [Em]life [G7]to [Dm]live, [F]our [Em/G]death [Am]to [C/G]die.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]We read [F/C]thy [G7/B]power [C]to bless [F]and save,
[C]E'en in [F/C]the [G7]darkness [C]of [F]the grave;
[C]Still [Em]more [G7]in [Dm]resurrection [C/G]light
[C]We [Em]read [G7]the [Dm]fullness [Em/G]of [Am]thy [C/G]might.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[C]O love [F/C]of [G7]God, [C]our shield [F]and stay
[C]Through all [F/C]the [G7]perils [C]of [F]our way!
[C]Eternal [Dm]love, [F]in [Em/G]thee [Am]we [C/G]rest,
[C]Forever [Dm]safe, [F]forever [C/G]blest.
{end_of_verse}
